{"results": [{"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-088", "score": 0.108, "document": "# FAM:SF-APPS-088 | Study family SF-APPS-088: Offensive-identity resilience: connector absence vs usage-matched others\n- observed_research_question: Offensive-identity resilience: connector absence vs usage-matched others\n- auto_outcome_status: supported\n- observed_hypothesis: Connector absence displaces team offensive identity (D_A) more than usage-matched non-organizer absence.\n- observed_result: Unmatched conn vs role D_A 0.2020 vs 0.1021, t=5.97 p=2.87e-08. Usage-matched vs role: paired dD_A +0.1151, P(conn>ctrl)=81.2%, t=6.35 p=7.35e-09 n=96. Vs terminal: +0.0777 t=2.37 p=0.0261 n=25.\n- auto_failure_mechanism: D_positive (no failure: positive result)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:small_sample\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:MECHANICAL_FLOOR\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER\n- observed_failure_evidence: Usage-matched connector vs role occupant identity break is large and significant (n=96). Licensed comparison excludes organizers.\n- observed_sample_and_power: n=96 matched pairs vs role; n=25 vs terminal; 908 player-seasons\n- auto_related_family: FAM:SF-PAP-014"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPA-050", "score": 0.105, "document": "# FAM:SF-APPA-050 | Study family SF-APPA-050: Superstar sequential suppression: opponent play before the star\n- observed_research_question: Superstar sequential suppression: opponent play before the star\n- auto_outcome_status: not a hypothesis test\n- observed_hypothesis: A specific opponent play type on the preceding possession suppresses each star's next-possession PPP relative to that star's baseline.\n- observed_result: PUTBACK is top suppressor for 6+ stars (e.g. D. Mitchell 1.178 to 0.884, d=-0.294, n_after=95; B. Beal d=-0.345 n=32; C. Holmgren d=-0.222 n=52). Other tops: TRANSITION (A. Davis -0.058), POST_UP (N. Jokic -0.075), PULL_ [cut; read_family for the full text]\n- auto_failure_mechanism: E_unclear (mechanism unclear from the records)\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:DRIFT_NONSTATIONARITY\n- observed_failure_evidence: No multiplicity correction; n_after is 32-95 for several PUTBACK cells vs thousands of baseline possessions.\n- observed_sample_and_power: 30 stars; min n_after=30\n- auto_validation_status: no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-TMP-005", "score": 0.103, "document": "# FAM:SF-TMP-005 | Study family SF-TMP-005: Final checks: Design 5 placebo, defensive H2-adjustment trait reliability, start-of-half dip\n- observed_research_question: Final checks: Design 5 placebo, defensive H2-adjustment trait reliability, start-of-half dip\n- auto_outcome_status: no result recorded\n- observed_hypothesis: There is a reliable defensive second-half adjustment trait and the Design 5 gap depends on the slump event.\n- observed_result: NOT_RECORDED\n- auto_failure_mechanism: E_unclear (mechanism unclear from the records)\n- observed_failure_evidence: No log saved.\n- observed_sample_and_power: NOT_RECORDED\n- auto_validation_status: same_pipeline_validation; evidence: TMP-005: 'split-half (odd/even game) reliability of team-season h2-h1 change; de'\n- auto_related_family: FAM:SF-CHT-064\n- observed_method: Split-half (odd/even game) reliability of team-season H2-H1 change; Design 5 on triggered vs non-triggered units; early-vs-rest possession dip.\n- observed_verdict: inconclusive\n- observed_failure_type: E_unclear\n- observed_notes: NOT_RECORDED\n- auto_confidence: low (0.15)"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-078", "score": 0.103, "document": "# FAM:SF-APPS-078 | Study family SF-APPS-078: Channel 2: possession ending state vs next 90-180s volume/points\n- observed_research_question: Channel 2: possession ending state vs next 90-180s volume/points\n- auto_outcome_status: not a hypothesis test\n- observed_hypothesis: A possession's ending state changes opponent points/possessions in the next 90-180s beyond ~0.01-0.02 PPP boundary drift.\n- observed_result: 90s vs MADE_DEAD: TURNOVER_LIVE dOppPts=+0.510 dNetPts=-0.306 (dOppPPP=+0.055, dOppPoss=+0.298); MISSED_DEAD dNetPts=-0.112; PUTBACK dNetPts=+0.078. Volume (dOppPoss), not PPP, carries most of the live-TO cost.\n- auto_failure_mechanism: E_unclear (mechanism unclear from the records)\n- observed_failure_evidence: No inferential tests in the core table; live TO raising opponent possession count is largely definitional (steal starts a break).\n- observed_sample_and_power: n=911968; MADE_DEAD n=354564\n- auto_validation_status: no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED\n- auto_related_family: FAM:SF-APPS-075\n- observed_verdict: descriptive"}], "n_results": 4}

Stage 2. Using the retrieval result above (follow-up tools are allowed within the tool budget), complete steps 4 to 9
and reply with the final action. Output schema (all fields required):
{
 "research_concepts": [
  "concept"
 ],
 "methodological_questions": [
  "question"
 ],
 "historical_evidence": [
  {
   "id": "identifier of a record returned by a tool",
   "status_as_recorded": "outcome status exactly as stated in the record (supported | rejected | inconclusive | untestable | artifact | not a hypothesis test | no result recorded)",
   "finding": "what the record states, in its own terms"
  }
 ],
 "failed_approaches": [
  {
   "id": "identifier of a returned record",
   "what_failed": "approach",
   "why": "failure mechanism or limitation as recorded"
  }
 ],
 "evidence_establishes": [
  "what the retrieved evidence establishes for this question"
 ],
 "evidence_does_not_establish": [
  "what it leaves open or cannot show"
 ],
 "own_inferences": [
  "your inference, not stated in any record"
 ],
 "uncertainties": [
  "uncertainty or missing information"
 ],
 "historical_effect": {
  "changed_decision": "yes | no | no_historical_evidence",
  "explanation": "whether and how the historical evidence changed the decision"
 },
 "testability": {
  "p_testable": "number in [0,1]: probability the question can be answered with the stated data at useful power",
  "blocking_constraints": [
   {
    "code": "one of RISK_CODES",
    "text": "string"
   }
  ]
 },
 "prior_work": {
